WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.620
PRESENTER: Stucco is one
of the oldest construction

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.390
materials on the planet.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:12.390
The earliest formulations
date back to ancient Greece

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:14.280
and Mayan Mexico.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.930
Stucco has stuck around.

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:19.860
And as an exterior siding,
it's come a long way.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.460
Modern stucco is more attractive
and offers better protection.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:30.230
Whether cement or
acrylic-based, stucco always

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.840
starts out as a sticky
paste, and that's

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.670
the great thing about stucco.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:37.070
In this wet and
gooey form, it can

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.250
be worked as it's applied to
the exterior of a building

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.005
to achieve a
variety of textures.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.640
It hardens to provide
a tough exterior

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.485
that shields the building
against the elements.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:55.290
To mass produce
cement stucco, they

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:57.120
start with tons of silica sand.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.460
They unload it into a
conveyor and elevator

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:05.400
system which delivers the
sand to silos for storage

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:06.200
until needed.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:11.740
They select sand with
various grades of coarseness

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:13.000
for different stucco finishes.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:17.940
They mix it with cement,
lime, and other ingredients

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.620
to create the stucco base.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:26.450
A technician demonstrates how
the ingredients come together

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:29.120
using this research lab mixer.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:31.400
She blends all the
ingredients dry,

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:35.060
achieving a consistency that's
similar to cake mix from a box.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.920
Cement stucco is
sold in dry form.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.290
Water will be added to
liquefy the ingredients

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:43.250
on the job site.

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:47.220
In this demonstration,
she also adds pigment.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.110
With a stucco
pre-colored, there's

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.550
no need to paint the building.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:01.650
To mass produce cement stucco,
they use this mega mixer.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:06.550
The operator adds three
or four different pigments

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:09.370
to create a custom color
in the dry stucco batch.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:14.570
Large paddle blades
spiral vigorously.

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:16.760
Usually, this is a
closed operation,

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:18.375
but they've opened
it up for our camera.

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:24.290
After three minutes of
mixing, the dry stucco mix

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:25.200
is ready for scrutiny.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:31.320
An employee takes a sample
and sends it to the quality

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.030
control lab for evaluation.

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:40.260
At the lab, the technician
weighs the stucco mixture

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.130
and adds water.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:48.140
He keeps an eye on the scale
to ensure that the amounts are

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:49.380
proportionate.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.310
He mixes them and
visually checks

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:57.740
to confirm that the
pigment and raw materials

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:58.850
are well dispersed.

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:02.060
Acrylic stucco,
on the other hand,

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:05.030
calls for an entirely
different recipe.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:07.130
They use calcium
carbonate instead

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:11.690
of silica sand and acrylic as
a binder instead of cement.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:14.810
They mix it with water and
sell it wet in a bucket

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:16.460
instead of dry.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.980
To color it, they use
a computerized tint

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:22.340
machine similar to what
you find in a paint store.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:24.740
They load the machine
with liquid pigments

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.860
and enter a color formula
into the computer.

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:32.880
It mixes the pigments to
produce the exact color,

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.040
and it releases the
precise amount needed.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.480
They blend the color
into the acrylic stucco,

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:41.820
and the batch ends up
looking like blue mud.

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:45.800
It's now ready to
apply to a home--

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:46.790
no prep required.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:53.100
They also sell acrylic
stucco with no color at all.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.610
It's called tint base.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:57.870
The pigments will be
added on the job site

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.300
where they can be
adjusted if needed.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:03.840
An airtight seal keeps the
stucco in its fascia state.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:08.070
Acrylic stucco dries
quickly like paint,

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:11.580
while cement stucco takes
28 days to totally cure

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:12.975
into a more durable finish.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.120
Over on the cement stucco
line, a rotating machine

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:20.100
handles all the packaging.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:23.130
A suctioning device pulls a
paper bag into position under

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:25.260
a spout which then fills it up.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.900
It takes just eight seconds
to fill a 90-pound bag.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:34.440
That works out to over
1,300 bags per hour--

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.495
enough material for 30 houses.

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:44.990
The machine transfers the
bag to the conveyor belt.

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:47.680
This stucco is now ready
to provide a strong finish

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.420
to building projects.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:52.300
Applied to a building's
exterior, stucco

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:55.330
can be textured to suit
the homeowner's taste,

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:59.120
and it will harden to provide
the building with a tough skin.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:03.780
That's why stucco continues to
be part of the urban landscape.

